Package: satrct
Type: Package
Title: Single-Arm Trials Versus Randomized Trials of the Same Size
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Gosuke", "Homma", , "gosuke.homma@astellas.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6854-5627"))
Description: Compares a single-arm trial, whose patients all receive the
    experimental treatment and are compared with an external control group or
    a fixed threshold, with a randomized controlled trial of the same total
    sample size. Provides the bias at which the two designs have equal mean
    squared error (Pocock (1976) <doi:10.1016/0021-9681(76)90044-8>;
    Collignon et al. (2020) <doi:10.1177/0962280219880213>), the power, type I
    error and sample size of a single-arm comparison with a prespecified bias
    margin, the relaxed significance level at which a randomized trial matches
    its power, hybrid designs with concurrent and external controls, and exact
    operating characteristics for binary endpoints.
